+\subsection{An interval-counting identity for the intrinsic energy}
+
+Let $Q$ be a stationary simple point process of intensity one with
+finite second count moments on bounded intervals. Its reduced second
+factorial moment measure $\alpha_Q$ is the locally finite positive
+measure on $\R$ characterized by
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:reduced-factorial-moment}
+\E_Q\sum_{\substack{x,y\in\gamma\\x\ne y}}\varphi(x,y)
+ =\int_\R\int_\R\varphi(x,x+h)\,\alpha_Q(\dd h)\dd x
+\end{equation}
+for every nonnegative compactly supported measurable function
+$\varphi$ on $\R^2$. The sum is over ordered pairs; simplicity gives
+$\alpha_Q(\{0\})=0$. No density of $\alpha_Q$ is assumed. Put
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:factorial-count-overlap}
+\begin{aligned}
+A_Q(t)&:=\E_Q\!\left[N_{(0,t]}\bigl(N_{(0,t]}-1\bigr)\right]
+       =v_Q(t)+t^2-t,\\
+A_Q(t)&=\int_\R(t-|h|)_+\,\alpha_Q(\dd h),\qquad t>0.
+\end{aligned}
+\end{equation}
+The second identity follows from \eqref{eq:reduced-factorial-moment}:
+for a fixed displacement $h$, the admissible first coordinates form
+an interval of length $(t-|h|)_+$.
+
+For $R>1$, define
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:intrinsic-energy}
+\begin{aligned}
+e_R(Q)&:=\int_{0<|h|<R}
+ \left(1-\frac{|h|}{R}\right)(-\log|h|)
+ \bigl(\alpha_Q(\dd h)-\dd h\bigr),\\
+W^{\rm int}(Q)&:=\liminf_{R\to\infty}e_R(Q).
+\end{aligned}
+\end{equation}
+The pair and Lebesgue-background terms are evaluated separately.
+For fixed $R$, the negative part is finite, so $e_R(Q)$ is well
+defined in $\R\cup\{+\infty\}$. Formula
+\eqref{eq:intrinsic-energy} is the one-dimensional logarithmic case
+of \cite[equation~(3.12)]{Leble}, with $g(h)=-\log|h|$ and no
+factor $1/2$ in the pair interaction.
 
